frac{125}{8} = 15.625 \\] (not an integer)\n\n9. If \\( a = 9 \\):\n   \\[ b = \\frac{19 \\cdot 9 - 3}{8} = \\frac{138}{8} = 17.25 \\] (not an integer)\n\nThe only valid solutions are \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( a = 7 \\), giving us the two-digit integers \\( 12 \\) and \\( 74 \\). The smallest of these two numbers is \\( 12 \\).\n\nTherefore, the smallest two-digit integer \\( n \\) such that switching its digits and then adding 3 results in \\( 2n \\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
